The family uses the [paper’s Theorem 3.1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.03358) reduction from Independent Set to IC-WCOL(1), with exact projective-line compatibility graphs.

Key results:

- `TRACK = "B"`
- Shipping preset: `medium` (`p=50021`, 11 answer vertices)
- All G1–G9 gates pass
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each
- Reference algorithm: 346,247 transitions and 0.95 seconds on average
- Compact route: at most 220 exact operations
- Bare oracle: 0/3 solved at shipping
- Structural hint: 1/3; placebo: 0/3
- Answer size: 133 characters, 22 atomic integers
- Emit smoke test successfully produced three JSONL instances

The README documents the important caveat that the enormous IC-WCOL graph is represented succinctly, so this is a no-tool compression benchmark rather than an explicit-graph complexity claim.
